A||||8||Alex4mula||Which digital camera  you recomend?||||1||
Z||000000||Alex4mula||03-06-2001||10:22 AM||||I'm looking to buy a new digital camera. My choice will be one with 3.3 MP resolution cause it will substitute my current APS.<BR>Which model do you recommend from experience? Also which service do you use to develop digital photos other than printing yourselves? Tks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tigger||03-06-2001||10:39 AM||||Sony Mavica Series, 1024x768 and 800x600 resolutions, can either fit about 15-20 of the 1024 size pictures, 20-25 of the 800, or a combination of the both on a single floppy disk.  Quick, easy, offload to any computer with a floppy drive, great resolution, decent zoom.  Long life lithium battery.<P><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerfiero1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerfiero1.jpg</A><P>Print (to an HP722C) using Kodak photo-paper and get picture quality results<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 03-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||03-06-2001||10:40 AM||||I only have a 1.8MP camera so I can't help you there. But I use a place called Wolf Camera to print out pics onto the real thicker photo paper. Any upper end camera shop can do prints. I've only did it twice. It's about the same cost per print as regular film. Usually I just print them out myself on photo paper.||||reg||1
Z||000003||WampusCat||03-06-2001||10:52 AM||||Olympus digitals alwas get great reviews.  I have the C-2100 ultra zoom.  It's kinda pricey but I love that 10X optical zoom with image stabilization.  It comes with USB interface so you don't need a card reader to quickly download images.  If you don't need the zoom, the other Oly's have great image quality.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||03-06-2001||11:23 AM||||for christmas i bought myself a Panasonic mdl#PV-SD4090 it has 35mm lens with zoom, 1280 X 960 pixels,  Takes JPEG,Quicktime moving videos, uses floppy disks 1.44mb or 120mb. Stores up to 1500 pics on one disk, has its own internal disk drive and USB hookup.has 2 inch LCD viewfinder/preview screen. Takes sound, rapid sequencing too. Not bad at $495. I can email the specifications sheet with all the data<P>I  dont like messing with memory cards, can just take disk out of camera and its ready for your disc drive in pc. also can preview 12 thumnails on camera LCD at a time to search for pics, can delete any 1 or all at any time.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 03-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||LarryB||03-06-2001||12:19 PM||||One feature I'd list as a must-have would be the USB interface, like a couple of the guys already alluded to.  You definitely do NOT want to be stuck using a serial interface to upload your images to your PC, otherwise you'll end up wanting to buy a card reader that can read the correct type of memory card for your camera.<P>I've had a Nikon Coolpix 900 for a couple of years and it takes outstanding pictures, but waiting nearly an hour to dump a days worth of photos doesn't cut it.  One of these days I'll pony up and get a card reader. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||SteveJ||03-06-2001||01:22 PM||||At the place I used to work we shared a Sony Mavica between 30 - 40 people ( a formula for disaster). We took 12,000 pictures in two years. When I retired in November it was still going strong.<BR>No breakdowns, fast charging, and no need for serial or USB. No expensive memory chips just cheap old floppies. . . and take pictures as long as you have more floppies.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Carrolles||03-06-2001||02:07 PM||||Olympus (I believe) makes a 3.4 MP camera with the new 340 megabyte IBM Micro Drive.  It will hold 250 max resolution pictures or 2000 economy resolution pictures.<P>The micro drive is a very tiny hard drive.  Popular Mechanics listed it as one of the year's best developements.<P>A friend has one and has printed 11x14s with near photo quality.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Alex4mula||03-06-2001||07:44 PM||||Wow! Thank you guys for the feedback. I thought that only Sony made floppy cameras. Now I know that Panasonic has one too. I like that idea but was told that the 1.2-2 mega-pixel resolution of them was not good for photo quality. I'll take a look at your choices. Thanks again.||||reg||1
